spec:
  grid: 16x16 (square, even-sized) [observed]
  symmetry_pattern:
    description: grid has full D4 (dihedral-4) symmetry -- invariant under LR flip, UD flip, 90/180/270 rotation, transpose, and anti-transpose
    fundamental_domain: upper-left triangle of upper-left 8x8 quadrant (36 cells where col <= row)
    colors: 6-8 distinct non-marker colors [observed]; no further structure (not concentric rings)
  marker_rect:
    color: a color not used in the underlying symmetric pattern; always 3 [observed]
    shape: 4x4 solid rectangle [observed]
    position: anywhere such that each covered cell has >=1 of its 3 reflections (LR, UD, 180) outside the marker rect
    constraint: marker color appears ONLY in this rectangle; does not straddle both center axes simultaneously [observed]
  output: the hidden patch under the marker rect, same size as the marker (4x4), obtained by copying the unique non-marker value from each cell's mirror counterpart

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first -- build the complete D4-symmetric grid, then overlay the marker
  steps:
    1. Choose grid size N=16 (even). Pick 6-8 distinct colors from 0-9 excluding the marker color.
    2. Fill the fundamental domain (36 cells in upper-left triangle of 8x8 quadrant) randomly with chosen colors.
    3. Reflect to build the full 16x16 D4-symmetric grid (LR + UD + transpose).
    4. Pick a marker color not in the palette (e.g. 3).
    5. Choose a random 4x4 rect position (r0, c0) such that every cell in the rect has >=1 of its 3 LR/UD/180 reflections outside the rect. Reject positions that straddle both center axes.
    6. Record the 4x4 patch as the expected output, then overwrite the rect with the marker color.
```
